  "reasoning": "The patient presents with a widespread itchy red rash ('red spots all over my body'), accompanied by systemic symptoms including fever, headache, and exhaustion. This combination of a generalized pruritic rash with febrile illness and fatigue is highly characteristic of a viral exanthem. Among the possible diagnoses, chicken pox specifically matches this clinical picture, as it commonly presents with an itchy, vesicular or maculopapular rash covering the body, along with prodromal fever, headache, and malaise. Conditions like allergies or fungal infections typically lack fever, while dengue usually features severe myalgia/arthralgia and bleeding risks rather than primarily itchy spots. Therefore, the symptom profile strongly aligns with chicken pox.",
  "final_answer": "[DIAGNOSIS]chicken pox[/DIAGNOSIS]"
}
